<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uganda National Liberation Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1979">1979</a>–<a href="/years/1986">1986</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Uganda National Liberation Army was the force of Ugandan exiles formed in 1979 to fight alongside the Tanzanian army against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a>, and it became Uganda's national army after his overthrow. Poorly disciplined and divided, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a>'s second government it fought the Bush War against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoweri-museveni">Yoweri Museveni</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-resistance-army">National Resistance Army</a>, committing widespread atrocities against civilians in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luwero-triangle">Luwero Triangle</a>. It disintegrated when the NRA took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampala">Kampala</a> in 1986.</p></div>
